<div id="show-message-upgrade-complete" class="hidden show-message">
    <div class="box">
        <div class="box-inner">
            <h2>Sprucemarks Continued</h2>

            <p>
                The original Sprucemarks by Kai Nightmode was archived in August 2026 and dedicated to the public domain. Sprucemarks Continued is an independent community fork that keeps it working and available. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the original author.
            </p>

            <p>
                Your options and sorting behave exactly as before. Source code, issues, and release notes are on <a href="https://github.com/vitorhmcorreia/sprucemarks-continued" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
            </p>

            <p>
                <input class="button show-message-dismiss" data-id="show-message-upgrade-complete" type="button" value="Continue">
            </p>
        </div><!-- box-inner -->
    </div><!-- box -->
</div><!-- show-message-upgrade-complete -->

<div id="show-message-chrome-extensions-toolbar" class="hidden show-message">
    <div class="box">
        <div class="box-inner">
            <p>
                Google Chrome hides extensions by default but you can use the extensions <span class="no-wrap">menu <img src="/images/messages/chrome/puzzle.png?version=2022.7.2.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon icon-chrome-puzzle" alt></span> in the upper right of Chrome to enable the <span class="no-wrap">pin <img src="/images/messages/chrome/pin.png?version=2022.7.2.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon icon-chrome-pin" alt></span> option for Sprucemarks Continued.
            </p>

            <p>
                The above procedure will allow the Sprucemarks Continued <span class="no-wrap">icon <img src="/images/messages/chrome/tree.png?version=2022.7.2.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon" alt></span> to be visible and enable one-click access.
            </p>

            <p>
                <input class="button show-message-dismiss" data-id="show-message-chrome-extensions-toolbar" type="button" value="Continue">
            </p>
        </div><!-- box-inner -->
    </div><!-- box -->
</div><!-- show-message-chrome-extensions-toolbar -->

<div id="show-message-edge-extensions-toolbar" class="hidden show-message">
    <div class="box">
        <div class="box-inner">
            <p>
                Microsoft Edge hides extensions by default but you can use the extensions <span class="no-wrap">menu <img src="/images/messages/edge/puzzle.png?version=2022.7.2.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon icon-edge-puzzle" alt></span> in the upper right of Edge to enable the <span class="no-wrap">eye <img src="/images/messages/edge/eye.png?version=2022.7.2.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon icon-edge-eye" alt></span> option for Sprucemarks Continued.
            </p>

            <p>
                The above procedure will allow the Sprucemarks Continued <span class="no-wrap">icon <img src="/images/messages/edge/tree.png?version=2022.7.2.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon" alt></span> to be visible and enable one-click access.
            </p>

            <p>
                <input class="button show-message-dismiss" data-id="show-message-edge-extensions-toolbar" type="button" value="Continue">
            </p>
        </div><!-- box-inner -->
    </div><!-- box -->
</div><!-- show-message-edge-extensions-toolbar -->

<div id="show-message-firefox-extensions-toolbar" class="hidden show-message">
    <div class="box">
        <div class="box-inner">
            <p>
                Mozilla Firefox hides extensions by default but you can use the extensions <span class="no-wrap">menu <img src="/images/messages/firefox/puzzle.png?version=2025.6.26.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon" alt></span> in the upper right of Firefox to click on the <span class="no-wrap">gear <img src="/images/messages/firefox/gear.png?version=2025.6.26.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon" alt></span> for Sprucemarks Continued which will then reveal a "Pin to Toolbar" option.
            </p>

            <p>
                The above procedure will allow the Sprucemarks Continued <span class="no-wrap">icon <img src="/images/messages/firefox/tree.png?version=2025.6.26.0" width="18" height="18" class="icon" alt></span> to be visible and enable one-click access.
            </p>

            <p>
                <input class="button show-message-dismiss" data-id="show-message-firefox-extensions-toolbar" type="button" value="Continue">
            </p>
        </div><!-- box-inner -->
    </div><!-- box -->
</div><!-- show-message-firefox-extensions-toolbar -->